<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Records Retention and Disposal</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Lifecycle management ensuring documents remain available for required periods then 
            dispose securely with proper authorization and documentation aligned with ISO 15489 
            and regulatory retention requirements.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Retention Schedule Configuration</h2>
        <p>
            Retention schedules define document lifespans based on regulatory requirements and 
            business needs. Financial records maintain seven-year retention for tax authority 
            compliance while employment records follow five-year statutory requirements. Custom 
            schedules accommodate industry-specific and organizational policies.
        </p>
        <p>
            Schedule assignment occurs automatically during document capture based on document 
            type and classification. Retention period calculation begins from document dates 
            with extensions for ongoing matters or legal proceedings.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Legal Hold and Litigation Support</h2>
        <p>
            Legal hold workflows freeze document disposal when litigation or investigation requires 
            preservation beyond normal retention periods. Hold notices cascade through document 
            categories ensuring comprehensive preservation without manual identification of affected 
            records.
        </p>
        <p>
            Hold management tracks which documents remain under preservation and for which matters. 
            Release workflows remove holds when preservation requirements expire allowing normal 
            retention processing to resume with appropriate documentation.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Secure Disposal and Certification</h2>
        <p>
            Automated retention expiry alerts notify records managers when documents reach disposal 
            eligibility. Review workflows verify no ongoing business need or legal hold applies 
            before authorizing destruction.
        </p>
        <p>
            Secure disposal processes overwrite or shred digital content preventing recovery even 
            with advanced forensic techniques. Destruction certificates document disposal completion 
            with details of destroyed records, authorization, and execution date supporting audit 
            requirements and legal defense.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

